, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Fixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so the built-in `round(x, 2)` rounds it down. The docstring promised half-up rounding, but the code never did that.\n\n**Fix** in `pricing/money.py`: the value is converted with `Decimal(str(x))` (`str` gives back the short form `\"2.675\"`), then rounded to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` and returned as a `float`. The return type doesn't change, so `add_vat` keeps working as before. Negative halves round away from zero (`-2.675` \u2192 `-2.68`).\n\n**Test:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, covering `2.675`, `1.005`, `0.125`, `2.674`, `-2.675` and an integer input. pytest isn't installed here, so I called the test functions directly with `python3`. The new test and the existing `test_split` both pass, and `add_vat(10)` still gives `12.0`.\n\n`add_vat` still does its multiplication in floats before rounding. A product that lands on an exact half-cent could pick up the same kind of error, which I left out of this fix.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 8, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 221752, "requests_cache_write": 6745, "requests_cost_usd": 0.11398740000000002, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 18, "requests_output": 1792, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial23", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 44, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T06:18:35.358838+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 25.638, "t_checker_s": 0.38, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-bugfix-regress", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_s